# Third-party source text. This pipeline reads a copyrighted screenplay to derive
# structure; it publishes results BY REFERENCE (offsets, digests, MinHash) and never
# copies the prose.
#
# The patterns match by filename ANYWHERE in the tree, not by directory. In the sibling
# storytree repo a narrower, directory-scoped pattern failed to cover a newly created
# run directory, a full screenplay was committed, and history had to be purged. Do not
# narrow these.
**/script.normalized.txt
**/script.raw.txt
**/matrix.txt
**/*_screenplay.txt
**/*screenplay*.txt
runs/**/*.txt
**/source/

# Third-party screenplay PDFs stay out. The rule is deliberately broad, so the one PDF that
# IS meant to ship needs an explicit exception rather than a narrowed rule — narrowing this
# pattern is how a full screenplay reached a commit in the sibling repository.
*.pdf
!reference/CogniTino-whitepaper.pdf

# Per-call logs carry full prompts, which contain source spans.
**/logs/
**/calls/
*.jsonl

# MCQ generation intermediates hold the scene excerpts questions were written from.
**/mcq_source_excerpts*.json
**/quarantine/
